file: "packages/editor/src/canvas/canvas.tsx"
doc: "The single SVG scene and its navigation and selection gestures."

constants: [
  { name: "Canvas"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Three changes. Everything else -- the pan/zoom group, the three\n"
      "layers, the pointer router wiring, the wheel handler, the keydown\n"
      "listener, the text editor, fit-on-load -- is untouched, and in\n"
      "particular the local `gesture` and `preview` signals that drive a\n"
      "POINTER drag stay exactly as they are.\n"
      "\n"
      "1. OverlayLayer's `preview` prop gains a second source. Today it is\n"
      "   fed the local `preview()` signal. It becomes a memo returning\n"
      "   modalPreview(props.ui.modalGesture(), geometry()) when a modal\n"
      "   gesture is open, and the local `preview()` otherwise.\n"
      "\n"
      "   The geometry() guard governs the MODAL branch only, because only\n"
      "   modalPreview takes geometry. A live pointer drag keeps yielding\n"
      "   its local `preview()` whether or not geometry() is defined, which\n"
      "   is what it does today and is not being changed.\n"
      "\n"
      "   So the memo yields undefined when no modal gesture is open and no\n"
      "   drag is in flight; when a modal gesture is open and either\n"
      "   geometry() is undefined or modalPreview returns undefined. That\n"
      "   is the existing meaning of the prop and needs no change in\n"
      "   OverlayLayer.\n"
      "\n"
      "2. `dimmedRefs` gains the same second source. It reads the local\n"
      "   `gesture()` signal and returns the moving or resizing refs so\n"
      "   DiagramLayer can fade the real elements under the preview outline.\n"
      "   For a modal gesture that local signal is undefined, so today\n"
      "   dimmedRefs would return the empty list and every element the\n"
      "   gesture targets would stay painted at full opacity beneath its own\n"
      "   preview outline.\n"
      "\n"
      "   When props.ui.modalGesture() is defined, take its `refs` for kind\n"
      "   'grab' -- all of them -- and for kind 'resize' its `refs[0]`,\n"
      "   which is its only ref because 'enter-resize' refuses to open a\n"
      "   gesture on any selection but a single element. Use that in place\n"
      "   of what the local signal would have given.\n"
      "\n"
      "   The callout-preview loop that dimmedRefs runs afterwards is\n"
      "   unchanged. It reads whichever preview is active, so it starts\n"
      "   firing for modal gestures as a consequence of change 1, with no\n"
      "   edit of its own.\n"
      "\n"
      "   Both memos take the modal gesture as the higher-precedence source,\n"
      "   so that within one gesture the dimmed set and the previewed set\n"
      "   are the same elements. Split precedence would fade one element and\n"
      "   outline another.\n"
      "\n"
      "3. `onPointerDown` clears any open modal gesture --\n"
      "   props.ui.setModalGesture(undefined) -- before anything else it\n"
      "   does. A press starts a pointer interaction, and the two must not\n"
      "   be live together: the memos above give the modal gesture\n"
      "   precedence, so a drag begun while a gesture was open would show no\n"
      "   preview at all and then commit normally on pointer-up, which is\n"
      "   the worst available combination. Note that onPointerDown runs no\n"
      "   command, so runCommand's clear does not cover this path.\n"
      "\n"
      "Taken together these three changes are what make the modal preview\n"
      "identical to the one a pointer drag of the same delta would show. A\n"
      "modal gesture and a pointer drag end in the SAME TWO PROPS --\n"
      "OverlayLayer's `preview` and DiagramLayer's `dimmed` -- and for the\n"
      "outline both reach them through moveUpdate or resizeUpdate in\n"
      "gestures/drag_machines.ts, one or the other according to the kind.\n"
      "Neither path computes an outline of its own."
    type: { named: { symbol: "Component", args: [{ named: { symbol: "CanvasProps" } }] } }
    uses: ["CanvasProps", "modalPreview", "ScenePreview", "ElementRef"]
  }
]
